I1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b471983de55989edd416f6b9fb45bdfc1df3b5b868ae8a9efcfeb51422d44c9f","event_uuid":"6c99a04a-d08c-43ff-82af-c82978974e10","position":{"commit_sha":"1343ef5b7eb44aca2474a59827a1c2c3d97afd24","position":"1786686964567379001-6c99a04a-d08c-43ff-82af-c82978974e10"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LIVE RECURRENCE (2026-08-14) under parallel multi-session writes, canonical\n/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker. Observed: HEAD ahead of origin/tickets by 4\nunpushed ticket commits (EDIT + FILE_IMPACT for cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3 + 2 \"Merge\norigin/tickets (auto-reconcile)\" merges), working tree dirty with 119 uncommitted .archived\ndeletions, 126 stray .write.lock files, zero .tmp-event-*. Recovery: `git checkout -- .`\nrestored the 119 tracked .archived (non-destructive; they exist on HEAD), tree went clean,\nthe stranded commits then converged to origin (ahead/behind 0/0). The dirty tree REAPPEARED\nwithin minutes — traced to a ticket CLOSE (cinderlike-lucky-akitainu in_progress->closed)\nwhose maybe_compact() spawned a detached sweep, concurrent with closes from other sessions\non unpatched code. This is abort variant (b) (tracked .archived deletions), DISTINCT from the\nuntracked-overwrite variant fixed by 1757 — evidence that compaction atomicity (this ticket)\nis required IN ADDITION to the reconverge-side recovery. Store re-recovered and healthy;\nparallel pickup agents paused on tracker writes pending durable fix.","timestamp":1786676405082452001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"OPERATIONAL STATUS + INTERIM MITIGATION APPLIED (2026-08-13 session cd66bacc).\n\nState check of the shared tracker: working tree CLEAN, ahead/behind origin = 0/0 (a prior session's recovery held or the deletions were committed). Latent exposure remains: 119 */.archived and 126 */.write.lock files are still TRACKED in HEAD (committed before the gitignore patterns), so any interrupted sweep re-creates abort variant (b).\n\nINTERIM MITIGATION now active machine-wide: compact.trigger = \"off\" set in the XDG user config (~/.config/rebar/config.toml). The project rebar.toml does not set compact.trigger, so user-level off governs every worktree/session on this machine (precedence: project > user, and project is silent). This removes the dirty-tree seed until the crash-atomicity fix here lands. REMOVE the user-config block when closing this ticket.\n\nFix program being structured as an epic covering: crash-atomic fold (this ticket), reconverge variant (b) recovery, push-recovery parity (sulfuryl-suicidal-osprey), untracking */.archived + */.write.lock from HEAD via a sanctioned migration, fsck/doctor self-heal tooling for this class, and active-only scan scoping with an override flag.","timestamp":1786677036631872001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"IMPLEMENTATION PLAN (session: Copilot CLI, worktree mantis-atomic-fold).\n\nDesign: intent-journal (commit-pending sentinel) crash atomicity, per the epic's amended child bullet.\n\n1. New module src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py:\n   - write_intent(tracker, ticket_id, snapshot_path, fold_files): atomic JSON record {ticket_id, snapshot (tracker-relative), sources (tracker-relative)} under <git-dir>/rebar-compact-intents/<ticket_id>.json — OUTSIDE the worktree, so the sentinel can never itself be tree dirt.\n   - discard(journal): idempotent unlink.\n   - pending_intents(tracker), recover_abandoned_folds(tracker) [caller holds the store write lock], recover_abandoned_folds_locked(tracker) [acquires it only when journals are pending].\n   - Recovery discrimination: a journal whose snapshot is already in HEAD = crash between commit and journal removal -> discard only. A journal whose snapshot is uncommitted = abandoned partial fold -> rename *.retired sources back, unlink the uncommitted snapshot, git reset the ticket dir (unstage a crash-after-add), discard. The retained SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT state (incomplete rollback in _retire_folded_sources) has NO journal by construction, so recovery never touches it — fsck --repair-snapshots stays its sole owner.\n\n2. compact_txn._compact_locked: extract the mutation tail into _apply_fold() which (a) writes the intent journal before the first worktree mutation (when committing), (b) wraps snapshot-write -> retire -> commit in try/except with whole-fold rollback on ANY exception or commit failure (rename-back + snapshot unlink + unstage), (c) discards the journal on every completed outcome including both _retire_folded_sources failure returns. Recovery preamble runs inside the lock at fold start.\n\n3. compact.py sweep: _sweep_one_ticket stops passing --no-commit (unless the operator passed it to compact-all), so each fold commits as ONE unit inside its own locked section — a killed sweep strands at most zero dirty folds instead of an entire uncommitted batch. compact_all_cli runs recover_abandoned_folds_locked() as its preamble. _commit_backfill still runs as a safety net but now pushes even when nothing is staged (per-ticket commits mean the batch stage is normally empty).\n\nWithheld-oracle tests (written FIRST, confirmed RED) in tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py: kill the fold (raise) at each intermediate step and assert `git status --porcelain` is clean; simulate SIGKILL (journal left behind) and assert the next sweep/compact converges the tree; assert recovery is idempotent; assert a successful fold still compacts and leaves no journal; assert the retained-SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT path is NOT reverted by recovery.","timestamp":1786683560081036001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Validation + mutation-testing record (pre-push):\n\nTests: tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py (9 new oracle tests) all green; tests/unit -k compact = 93 passed / 4 skipped; interfaces compaction suite (incl. real-SIGKILL test_compact_process_death.py) + test_lock_holder_labelling.py = 36 passed. make lint PASS (complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0); make typecheck PASS (537 files). tests/integration/test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py shows 7 fixture-setup errors on this machine (git init --bare remote fails, exit 128) — verified identical at pristine origin/main, environmental and unrelated.\n\nManual mutation pass on the new/changed code (mutmut not in venv), 6 representative mutants, each confirmed killed by at least one oracle test, then reverted:\n- M1 skip journal write in _apply_fold -> KILLED (recovery test: abandoned fold not converged)\n- M2 skip _abort_fold on exception -> KILLED (dirty-tree-after-exception test)\n- M3 invert rollback all-renames-clean guard in _rollback_fold -> KILLED (snapshot retained/deleted wrong way)\n- M4 invert snapshot-in-HEAD revert guard in recover_abandoned_folds -> KILLED (committed fold wrongly reverted)\n- M5 skip snapshot unlink in _revert_partial_fold -> KILLED (tree not clean post-recovery)\n- M6 sweep always passes --no-commit -> KILLED (mid-sweep dirty-window test)\n\nResult: 6/6 mutants killed; no mutant code remains in the tree.","timestamp":1786684643229030001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 1763 patch set 2 pushed. Addressed LLM-Review PS1 findings:\n- BLOCKING bugfix-size-attestation: ran rebar review-plan on this bug -> PASS, signed at origin/main 27b868b; commit rebased onto that base (PS2 parent = 27b868b).\n- Advisory correctness: _snapshot_in_head is now tri-state (True/False/None); an unresolvable HEAD or rc-124 timeout reads INDETERMINATE and recovery KEEPS the journal (defers) instead of misreading a transient git fault as absent-from-HEAD and reverting a landed fold.\n- Advisory test gaps: 4 new oracle tests (13 total, all green) — snapshot-gone-from-disk discard branch, indeterminate-probe deferral (rc-124), write_intent-fails refusal (fold returns 1 with zero mutation), and the incomplete-rollback data-loss guard (snapshot RETAINED when a reverse-rename fails, removed when rollback is clean).\n- Mutation M7 (rc-124 treated as absent) confirmed KILLED. lint/typecheck/compact suite re-run green (97 passed, 4 skipped).","timestamp":1786685880880402001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PS3 review PASS (LLM-Review +1); addressed its 3 advisory findings in PS4:\n- correctness: _revert_partial_fold now mirrors _rollback_fold's data-loss guard — the snapshot is removed only when every reverse-rename succeeded; a stuck *.retired source retains the snapshot as SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT for fsck --repair-snapshots (journal still discarded so recovery never revisits fsck territory).\n- tests: added unresolvable-HEAD indeterminate-branch test, recovery retain-guard test, and lock-unavailable defer-contract test (16 oracle tests total, all green).\n- mutation M8 (invert the recovery retain guard) confirmed KILLED. lint/typecheck/raw-git gate all green.\nAlso PS1 CI failure root cause: the raw-git-writes gate required inline \"# raw-git-ok:\" markers on the two git-reset call lines (fixed in PS3).","timestamp":1786686964567379001}],"created_at":1786675020962002001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9db6e20f-56d9-496a-a30a-aa5d810063b0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6ccc-0577-198c-44fa"},{"link_uuid":"5bf5307a-9345-43ec-8c77-f179ff697b24","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f4a0-c986-5ab9-4a33"},{"link_uuid":"613822f1-792c-41a6-9e67-742f0931fb85","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b139-a155-f103-4940"},{"link_uuid":"da8e80aa-eb64-46e5-9c2c-d46ebb9c7c5e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f9d7-584c-2921-433e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe operation-linked compaction sweep is not crash-atomic, and this is the root wedge-generator for the store (parent epic becoming-berserk-grunion; live wedges recorded on e72e-259d-5ee7-4e73 and 6ccc-0577-198c-44fa). rebar._commands.compact_trigger.maybe_compact() fires on the tail of every ticket CLOSE and spawns a DETACHED sweep worker (run_sweep → compact.compact_all_cli → compact_txn). The fold performs snapshot-write → retire-rename (tracked source → `*.retired`) → git commit as SEPARATE steps with no rollback. If the detached worker dies, is killed, or races a concurrent writer between the rename and the commit, the SHARED tracker working tree is left DIRTY: tracked deletions plus untracked `*-SNAPSHOT.json` / `*.retired` files. A dirty tree then aborts the next reconverge union merge (\"local changes / untracked files would be overwritten\"), stranding local ticket commits — the chronic wedge. Interim mitigation `[compact] trigger=\"off\"` is active on the affected host and must be removable once this lands.\n\n## Approach\nMake the fold crash-atomic with an intent journal + rollback + startup recovery (the classic write-ahead-intent pattern):\n1. **Intent journal**: before mutating anything, `_apply_fold` writes a journal record (ticket dir, snapshot path, sources to retire) to a store-local journal location; if the journal cannot be written, the fold REFUSES (logs, stderr Error, exit 1) without mutating the store.\n2. **Ordered mutation + rollback**: perform snapshot-write, then renames, then ONE commit; on any failure after mutation begins, `_rollback_fold` reverse-renames and removes the uncommitted snapshot. If a reverse-rename itself fails (incomplete rollback), RETAIN the uncommitted snapshot rather than delete it — dropping it would lose folded events; the retained state is exactly what fsck reports as SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT and doctor can repair.\n3. **Recovery**: compact_recovery.recover_abandoned_folds scans for journals with no matching commit at startup/next sweep entry, discriminating: journal + uncommitted artifacts present → revert (restore sources, remove snapshot, clear journal); journal whose snapshot already reached HEAD → clear journal (fold landed); journal whose snapshot is gone from disk (superseded or fsck-repaired) → clear journal without touching ticket files.\n4. Transient-fault discipline: git probes used for discrimination must distinguish \"object absent\" from transient failures (index.lock contention, timeout) so recovery never mis-classifies a transient fault as \"snapshot absent\" and reverts a landed fold.\nThe journal lives with the store and is cleaned in the same locked scope as the fold; the sweep remains operation-linked (portable — no CI dependence).\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py — intent journal write, ordered fold, `_rollback_fold` with the retain-on-incomplete-rollback guard.\n- src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py — abandoned-fold discrimination + recovery.\n- src/rebar/_commands/compact.py — recovery invocation at sweep entry.\n- tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py (new) — kill-at-each-step coverage.\n- tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py — lock label update.\n\n## Testing\n- Crash injection at each step boundary (after journal, after snapshot-write, after renames, before commit): the next sweep entry recovers to a clean tree (`git status --porcelain` empty) with no ticket events lost.\n- Refusal path: journal write failure → exit 1, store untouched (zero mutations, zero commits).\n- Incomplete rollback: a failing reverse-rename retains the uncommitted snapshot; assert the snapshot bytes survive and fsck reports the state.\n- Recovery discrimination: landed-fold journal is cleared without reverting; superseded/fsck-repaired journal (snapshot gone from disk) is cleared without touching ticket files; transient git failure during the probe does NOT trigger a revert.\n- Idempotence: recovery on a clean store makes zero changes; double recovery is safe.\n- Manual mutation pass over journal/rollback/recovery branches; every mutant killed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A fold killed at ANY step boundary leaves a store that the next sweep entry converges to clean (no dirty tracked deletions, no stray snapshots, no lost events); checked by the crash-injection tests.\n- [ ] A fold that cannot journal refuses without mutating the store; checked by the refusal test.\n- [ ] Recovery never deletes folded-event bytes: incomplete rollback retains the snapshot, and landed/superseded journals are cleared without reverting ticket files; checked by the discrimination tests.\n- [ ] Transient git faults during recovery probes are not treated as \"snapshot absent\"; checked by the fault-injection test.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close; after merge the `[compact] trigger=\"off\"` mitigation is removed on the affected host.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","reason":"crash-atomic fold (journal+rollback)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py","reason":"abandoned-fold recovery"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"fold entry wiring"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_compact_crash_atomicity.py","reason":"crash-atomicity coverage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py","reason":"lock label update"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","fb8a-7363-e406-4e36"],["relates_to","b139-a155-f103-4940"],["relates_to","f4a0-c986-5ab9-4a33"],["relates_to","f9d7-584c-2921-433e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"fb8a-7363-e406-4e36","parent_status_uuid":"f7194906-8828-4153-b4de-c03772ebcc7c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e72e-259d-5ee7-4e73","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Defense-in-depth: make compaction crash-atomic — detached sweep that dies after write/retire but before commit leaves the tracker tree dirty (source of the untracked leftovers that wedge reconverge)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9fef9d3e-8e40-4dfe-8a33-68daa28d2b40","9db6e20f-56d9-496a-a30a-aa5d810063b0","ef3ca982-d49d-48c5-aff5-f7bcb99ecd59","53dc15e4-c374-4363-8736-ec6431e7e6bb","aec55542-73fb-42bf-975e-299f773a3635","908f406b-d089-4f96-87df-0c0b26ce55e3","f7194906-8828-4153-b4de-c03772ebcc7c","9b650a65-aa66-4161-a343-a504f29f8abf","814c3419-169c-4c46-bba6-8446af7fe55a","a283b8c9-ba1f-4421-af4a-9695ae8b355a","5bf5307a-9345-43ec-8c77-f179ff697b24","cb3be015-a549-4a9e-9b3f-410e97b65cd9","ea5f7493-c8ec-4d41-af01-fa87bb0e80ac","1072f847-ac06-4f71-b4c3-3bab5924db7b","80f25f68-d19e-4a0f-a392-c7c62cbaaa58","09a3b9a3-77dd-4ad9-aba8-50e48c19c958","613822f1-792c-41a6-9e67-742f0931fb85","da8e80aa-eb64-46e5-9c2c-d46ebb9c7c5e","6c99a04a-d08c-43ff-82af-c82978974e10"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786686964567379002,"uuid":"8827429c-257b-4ac9-8774-a7e67d2cf942"}